{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the waters prevailed a hundred and fifty days</b> — because the springs had burst forth and there was also rain falling one day and ceasing one day, for the meaning of \"I will cause it to rain\" (Genesis 7:4) is continuously without interruption, and the proof is that it says, \"and the rain was restrained\" (Genesis 8:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:41.398480514Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}